   "status": "UNCLEAR",
   "ruling": "Ruling: representation; i1040gi p. 90, worksheet line 6: \"Multiply the number of boxes checked by $1,550 ($1,950 if your 2024 filing status was single or head of household)\" and its footnote \"*If your filing status is married filing separately, you can check the boxes for your spouse only if your spouse had no income, isn’t filing a return, and can’t be claimed as a dependent on another person’s return\"; p. 33, Line 12d: \"Don’t check any boxes for your spouse if your filing status is head of household\". Each per-box helper is refund.per_box when its box is checked and zero otherwise, and refund.per_box is $1,550, or $1,950 when the 2024 status was single or head of household (refund.box_married, refund.box_unmarried), so the sum is the number of boxes times the amount. The married filing separately condition for the spouse boxes is in the spouse questions themselves (refund.spouse_born, refund.spouse_blind: \"answer yes only if your spouse also had no income, wasn't filing a return, and couldn't be claimed as a dependent on another person's return\"), as the footnote says; zeroing the spouse boxes for single, head of household and qualifying surviving spouse is the recorded reading amb.2025.refund_boxes_2024. Unchanged by the backlog packages.",
